(date's unit tests - the library gating itself, in this repo, with Vox as
 its only dependency, following the json library's own pattern exactly.

 Every value GNU date can produce is taken from GNU: the command that
 produced it sits beside the claim as a comment, run as

   TZ=UTC LC_ALL=C date -u -d '<when>' '+<format>'

 so the suite is a fidelity check against the reference and not against
 the author's own reading of it. Two departures from GNU are documented
 in README.md and tested against this library's OWN rule instead:
 'months later' and 'years later' clamp the day of month rather than
 overflowing into the next month, and there is no time zone but UTC.

   vox date.vox --shared -o libdate.so
   vox date_tests.vox --link date -o date_tests
   ./date_tests)

see date version "0.1" from "./libdate.lib".

a number called 'assertions made' is 0.
a number called failures is 0.

To check with a text called name and a text called wanted and a text called got.
  increment 'assertions made'.
  If got is wanted then, Return.
  increment failures.
  Print "ASSERT {name}: expected {wanted} got {got}".

(A text literal cannot sit inside a format hole that is itself inside a
 text literal - {'f' of "x"} cannot be written as "{'f' of "x"}" - so a
 claim about a number or a boolean takes the values themselves, unquoted,
 and stringifies them here instead of at the call site.)
To 'check moment' with a text called name and a number called wanted and a number called got.
  check with name and "{wanted}" and "{got}".

To 'check boolean' with a text called name and a boolean called wanted and a boolean called got.
  check with name and "{wanted}" and "{got}".

Print "-- now --".
a number called 'the current moment' is 'the moment now'.
a boolean called 'it is after today started' is false.
(the day this suite was written; a passing run can only be later)
If 'the current moment' is greater than 1758931200 then, set 'it is after today started' to true.
check with "the moment now is after 2026-09-27" and "1" and "{'it is after today started'}".
a number called 'the moment now again' is 'the moment now'.
a boolean called 'it did not go backwards' is false.
If 'the moment now again' is greater than or equal to 'the current moment' then, set 'it did not go backwards' to true.
check with "the moment now never goes backwards" and "1" and "{'it did not go backwards'}".

Print "-- civil time to a moment --".
(date -u -d '1970-01-01' +%s -> 0)
check with "the moment of the epoch date" and "0" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 1 and 1}".
(date -u -d '2026-07-29' +%s -> 1785283200)
check with "the moment of 2026-07-29" and "1785283200" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 29}".
(date -u -d '1969-12-31' +%s -> -86400)
check with "the moment of the day before the epoch" and "-86400" and "{'the moment of' with 1969 and 12 and 31}".
(date -u -d '2026-07-29 16:02:48' +%s -> 1785340968)
check with "the moment at a clock time" and "1785340968" and "{'the moment at' with 2026 and 7 and 29 and 16 and 2 and 48}".
(mktime-style overflow: day 0 is the last day of the previous month)
check with "day 0 is the last day of the previous month" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 1 and 31}" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 2 and 0}".
(day 32 of January is 1 February)
check with "day 32 of january is 1 february" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 2 and 1}" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 1 and 32}".
(month 13 is January of the next year)
check with "month 13 is january of the next year" and "{'the moment of' with 1971 and 1 and 1}" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 13 and 1}".
(month 0 is December of the previous year)
check with "month 0 is december of the previous year" and "{'the moment of' with 1969 and 12 and 1}" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 0 and 1}".
(hour 24 is midnight tomorrow)
check with "hour 24 is midnight tomorrow" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 1 and 2}" and "{'the moment at' with 1970 and 1 and 1 and 24 and 0 and 0}".
(a negative day of month steps back further still)
check with "day -1 of march is 27 february (1970 not a leap year)" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 2 and 27}" and "{'the moment of' with 1970 and 3 and -1}".

Print "-- a moment to its parts --".
(date -u -d '@0' '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %u %j' -> 1970-01-01 00:00:00 4 001)
check with "year of the epoch" and "1970" and "{'the year of' of 0}".
check with "month of the epoch" and "1" and "{'the month of' of 0}".
check with "day of month of the epoch" and "1" and "{'the day of month of' of 0}".
check with "hour of the epoch" and "0" and "{'the hour of' of 0}".
check with "minute of the epoch" and "0" and "{'the minute of' of 0}".
check with "second of the epoch" and "0" and "{'the second of' of 0}".
check with "weekday of the epoch (thursday)" and "4" and "{'the weekday of' of 0}".
check with "day of year of the epoch" and "1" and "{'the day of year of' of 0}".
(date -u -d '@-1' '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %u %j' -> 1969-12-31 23:59:59 3 365)
check with "year the second before the epoch" and "1969" and "{'the year of' of -1}".
check with "month the second before the epoch" and "12" and "{'the month of' of -1}".
check with "day of month the second before the epoch" and "31" and "{'the day of month of' of -1}".
check with "hour the second before the epoch" and "23" and "{'the hour of' of -1}".
check with "minute the second before the epoch" and "59" and "{'the minute of' of -1}".
check with "second the second before the epoch" and "59" and "{'the second of' of -1}".
check with "weekday the second before the epoch (wednesday)" and "3" and "{'the weekday of' of -1}".
check with "day of year the second before the epoch" and "365" and "{'the day of year of' of -1}".
(date -u -d '@-86400' '+%Y-%m-%d %u %j' -> 1969-12-31 3 365)
check with "day before the epoch, day of month" and "31" and "{'the day of month of' of -86400}".
(date -u -d '2026-07-29 16:02:48' '+%Y %m %d %H %M %S %u %j' -> 2026 07 29 16 02 48 3 210)
a number called 'a fixed moment' is 1785340968.
check with "year of the fixed moment" and "2026" and "{'the year of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "month of the fixed moment" and "7" and "{'the month of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "day of month of the fixed moment" and "29" and "{'the day of month of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "hour of the fixed moment" and "16" and "{'the hour of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "minute of the fixed moment" and "2" and "{'the minute of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "second of the fixed moment" and "48" and "{'the second of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "weekday of the fixed moment (wednesday)" and "3" and "{'the weekday of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "day of year of the fixed moment" and "210" and "{'the day of year of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
(date -u -d '2026-07-29 16:02:48' '+%V %G %q %C' -> 31 2026 3 20)
check with "iso week of the fixed moment" and "31" and "{'the iso week of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "iso week year of the fixed moment" and "2026" and "{'the iso week year of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "quarter of the fixed moment" and "3" and "{'the quarter of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
check with "century of the fixed moment" and "20" and "{'the century of' of 'a fixed moment'}".
(date -u -d '2024-02-29' '+%j %u %V' -> 060 4 09; a leap day. A hole cannot
 hold its own nested {...} sub-expression - the interpolation scanner
 closes at the first inner '}' and leaves the second as a stray literal
 character - so each moment is named first throughout this file.)
a number called 'leap day 2024' is {'the moment of' with 2024 and 2 and 29}.
check with "leap day of year" and "60" and "{'the day of year of' of 'leap day 2024'}".
check with "leap day weekday (thursday)" and "4" and "{'the weekday of' of 'leap day 2024'}".
check with "leap day iso week" and "9" and "{'the iso week of' of 'leap day 2024'}".
(date -u -d '2026-12-31' '+%j %u %V %G' -> 365 4 53 2026)
a number called '31 december 2026' is {'the moment of' with 2026 and 12 and 31}.
check with "31 december day of year" and "365" and "{'the day of year of' of '31 december 2026'}".
check with "31 december iso week" and "53" and "{'the iso week of' of '31 december 2026'}".
check with "31 december iso week year" and "2026" and "{'the iso week year of' of '31 december 2026'}".
(date -u -d '2027-01-01' '+%j %u %V %G' -> 001 5 53 2026 - 1 January belonging to the previous year's week 53)
a number called '1 january 2027' is {'the moment of' with 2027 and 1 and 1}.
check with "1 january day of year" and "1" and "{'the day of year of' of '1 january 2027'}".
check with "1 january 2027 iso week (previous year's 53rd)" and "53" and "{'the iso week of' of '1 january 2027'}".
check with "1 january 2027 iso week year" and "2026" and "{'the iso week year of' of '1 january 2027'}".
(date -u -d '2024-12-31' '+%V %G' -> 01 2025 - 31 December belonging to next year's week 1)
a number called '31 december 2024' is {'the moment of' with 2024 and 12 and 31}.
check with "31 december 2024 iso week (next year's 1st)" and "1" and "{'the iso week of' of '31 december 2024'}".
check with "31 december 2024 iso week year" and "2025" and "{'the iso week year of' of '31 december 2024'}".
(date -u -d '2000-01-01' '+%u %q %C'; date -u -d '1999-12-31' '+%u %q %C')
a number called '1 january 2000' is {'the moment of' with 2000 and 1 and 1}.
a number called '31 december 1999' is {'the moment of' with 1999 and 12 and 31}.
check with "quarter of january" and "1" and "{'the quarter of' of '1 january 2000'}".
check with "quarter of december" and "4" and "{'the quarter of' of '31 december 1999'}".
check with "century 1999" and "19" and "{'the century of' of '31 december 1999'}".

Print "-- names --".
check with "month name 7" and "July" and "{'the month name of' of 7}".
check with "short month name 7" and "Jul" and "{'the short month name of' of 7}".
check with "month name 1" and "January" and "{'the month name of' of 1}".
check with "month name 12" and "December" and "{'the month name of' of 12}".
check with "month name out of range low" and "" and "{'the month name of' of 0}".
check with "month name out of range high" and "" and "{'the month name of' of 13}".
check with "short month name out of range" and "" and "{'the short month name of' of 0}".
check with "weekday name 3" and "Wednesday" and "{'the weekday name of' of 3}".
check with "short weekday name 3" and "Wed" and "{'the short weekday name of' of 3}".
check with "weekday name 1" and "Monday" and "{'the weekday name of' of 1}".
check with "weekday name 7" and "Sunday" and "{'the weekday name of' of 7}".
check with "weekday name out of range" and "" and "{'the weekday name of' of 0}".
check with "short weekday name out of range" and "" and "{'the short weekday name of' of 8}".

Print "-- calendar facts --".
check with "2000 is a leap year (divides by 400)" and "1" and "{'is a leap year' of 2000}".
check with "1900 is not a leap year (divides by 100 not 400)" and "0" and "{'is a leap year' of 1900}".
check with "2024 is a leap year" and "1" and "{'is a leap year' of 2024}".
check with "2023 is not a leap year" and "0" and "{'is a leap year' of 2023}".
check with "2026 is not a leap year" and "0" and "{'is a leap year' of 2026}".
check with "days in february of a leap year" and "29" and "{'the days in' of 2 and 2024}".
check with "days in february of a common year" and "28" and "{'the days in' of 2 and 2023}".
check with "days in april" and "30" and "{'the days in' of 4 and 2026}".
check with "days in january" and "31" and "{'the days in' of 1 and 2026}".
check with "29 february 2024 is valid" and "1" and "{'is a valid date' of 2024 and 2 and 29}".
check with "29 february 2023 is not valid" and "0" and "{'is a valid date' of 2023 and 2 and 29}".
check with "month 13 is not a valid date" and "0" and "{'is a valid date' of 2026 and 13 and 1}".
check with "month 0 is not a valid date" and "0" and "{'is a valid date' of 2026 and 0 and 1}".
check with "day 0 is not a valid date" and "0" and "{'is a valid date' of 2026 and 1 and 0}".
check with "day 32 of january is not a valid date" and "0" and "{'is a valid date' of 2026 and 1 and 32}".
check with "23:59:59 is a valid time" and "1" and "{'is a valid time' of 23 and 59 and 59}".
check with "24:00:00 is not a valid time" and "0" and "{'is a valid time' of 24 and 0 and 0}".
check with "12:60:00 is not a valid time" and "0" and "{'is a valid time' of 12 and 60 and 0}".
check with "12:00:60 is not a valid time" and "0" and "{'is a valid time' of 12 and 0 and 60}".
check with "a negative hour is not a valid time" and "0" and "{'is a valid time' of -1 and 0 and 0}".

Print "-- moving around the calendar --".
a number called 'the fixed moment' is 1785340968.
check with "one second later" and "{'the fixed moment' add 1}" and "{'seconds later' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}".
check with "one second earlier" and "{'the fixed moment' subtract 1}" and "{'seconds later' of 'the fixed moment' and -1}".
check with "one minute later" and "{'the fixed moment' add 60}" and "{'minutes later' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}".
check with "one hour later" and "{'the fixed moment' add 3600}" and "{'hours later' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}".
check with "one day later" and "{'the fixed moment' add 86400}" and "{'days later' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}".
check with "one week later" and "{'the fixed moment' add 604800}" and "{'weeks later' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}".
(GNU overflows a month past January into March: date -u -d '2026-01-31 + 1 month' -> 2026-03-03. This library clamps instead - the documented departure.)
a number called 'the 31st of january 2026' is {'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 31}.
check with "31 january plus one month clamps to 28 february (2026 not a leap year)" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 2 and 28}" and "{'months later' of 'the 31st of january 2026' and 1}".
a number called 'the 31st of january 2024' is {'the moment of' with 2024 and 1 and 31}.
check with "31 january 2024 plus one month clamps to 29 february (a leap year)" and "{'the moment of' with 2024 and 2 and 29}" and "{'months later' of 'the 31st of january 2024' and 1}".
a number called 'the 29th of february 2024' is {'the moment of' with 2024 and 2 and 29}.
check with "29 february plus one year clamps to 28 february" and "{'the moment of' with 2025 and 2 and 28}" and "{'years later' of 'the 29th of february 2024' and 1}".
a number called 'a quarter past nine on 15 january 2026' is {'the moment at' with 2026 and 1 and 15 and 9 and 30 and 0}.
check with "a month later keeps the time of day" and "{'the moment at' with 2026 and 2 and 15 and 9 and 30 and 0}" and "{'months later' of 'a quarter past nine on 15 january 2026' and 1}".
check with "twelve months later is one year later" and "{'years later' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}" and "{'months later' of 'the fixed moment' and 12}".
a number called 'the 29th of july 2026' is {'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 29}.
check with "a negative count of months goes back" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 6 and 29}" and "{'months later' of 'the 29th of july 2026' and -1}".
check with "start of the day" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 29}" and "{'the start of the day of' of 'the fixed moment'}".
check with "start of the week (monday on or before a wednesday)" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 27}" and "{'the start of the week of' of 'the fixed moment'}".
check with "start of the month" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 1}" and "{'the start of the month of' of 'the fixed moment'}".
check with "start of the year" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 1}" and "{'the start of the year of' of 'the fixed moment'}".
check with "the weekday on or after, already that day" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 29}" and "{'the weekday on or after' of 'the fixed moment' and 3}".
check with "the weekday on or after, the next monday" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 8 and 3}" and "{'the weekday on or after' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}".
check with "the weekday on or before, already that day" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 29}" and "{'the weekday on or before' of 'the fixed moment' and 3}".
check with "the weekday on or before, the previous monday" and "{'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 27}" and "{'the weekday on or before' of 'the fixed moment' and 1}".
a number called 'the 1st of january 2026' is {'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 1}.
a number called 'the 10th of january 2026' is {'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 10}.
check with "days between, later minus earlier" and "9" and "{'the days between' of 'the 1st of january 2026' and 'the 10th of january 2026'}".
check with "days between, negative when the second is earlier" and "-9" and "{'the days between' of 'the 10th of january 2026' and 'the 1st of january 2026'}".
check with "days between is floored, not rounded" and "0" and "{'the days between' of 0 and 3600}".

Print "-- writing a moment out: every specifier --".
(date -u -d '2026-07-29 16:02:48' '+%Y|%m|%d|%H|%M|%S|%y|%j|%V|%G|%q|%C|%u|%a|%A|%b|%B|%p|%P|%z|%Z|%s|%e|%k|%l|%I|%r|%R|%T|%D|%F|%x|%X|%c|%h|%w|%U|%W|%g')
check with "%Y" and "2026" and {'the moment written as' of 'the fixed moment' and "%Y"}.
check with "%m" and "07" and {'the moment written as' of 'the fixed moment' and "%m"}.
check with "%d" and "29" and {'the moment written as' of 'the fixed moment' and "%d"}.
check with "%H" and "16" and {'the moment written as' of 'the fixed moment' and "%H"}.
