Print "-- round trips --".
a text called 'the fixed moment written out' is 'the date and time of' of 'the fixed moment'.
check with "the fixed moment survives a full write and read" and "{'the fixed moment'}" and "{'the moment read from' of 'the fixed moment written out'}".
a text called 'the epoch written as rfc 3339' is 'the rfc 3339 date and time of' of 0.
check with "the epoch survives rfc 3339" and "0" and "{'the moment read from' of 'the epoch written as rfc 3339'}".
a text called 'the day before the epoch written out' is 'the date and time of' of -86400.
check with "a moment before the epoch survives a round trip" and "-86400" and "{'the moment read from' of 'the day before the epoch written out'}".
a number called '1 january 2026 again' is {'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 1}.
a text called '1 january 2026 written out' is 'the date of' of '1 january 2026 again'.
check with "the date-only form survives a round trip" and "{'1 january 2026 again'}" and "{'the moment read from' of '1 january 2026 written out'}".
a number called 'the fixed moment read back once' is 'the moment read from' of 'the fixed moment written out'.
a text called 'the fixed moment written out twice' is 'the date and time of' of 'the fixed moment read back once'.
check with "a moment written and read twice is unchanged" and "{'the fixed moment'}" and "{'the moment read from' of 'the fixed moment written out twice'}".

Print "{'assertions made'} assertions, {failures} failures".
If failures is greater than 0 then, exit 1.
